Here's how to handle all three requirements:

### 1. Detect the Current System Theme

```csharp
AppTheme currentTheme = Application.Current!.RequestedTheme;
// Returns AppTheme.Light, AppTheme.Dark, or AppTheme.Unspecified
```

### 2. Subscribe to Real-Time Theme Changes

```csharp
// In your App constructor or page startup:
Application.Current!.RequestedThemeChanged += (s, e) =>
{
    AppTheme newTheme = e.RequestedTheme;

    // Log the change
    Debug.WriteLine($"System theme changed to: {newTheme}");

    // Update UI (e.g., swap ResourceDictionaries)
    ApplyTheme(newTheme == AppTheme.Dark
        ? new DarkTheme()
        : new LightTheme());
};
```

### 3. Let the User Force a Theme

```csharp
// Force dark mode regardless of OS
Application.Current!.UserAppTheme = AppTheme.Dark;

// Force light mode
Application.Current!.UserAppTheme = AppTheme.Light;

// Reset to follow system theme
Application.Current!.UserAppTheme = AppTheme.Unspecified;
```

Persist the choice so it survives restarts:

```csharp
// Save
Preferences.Set("AppTheme", "Dark");

// Restore on startup
var saved = Preferences.Get("AppTheme", "System");
Application.Current!.UserAppTheme = saved switch
{
    "Light" => AppTheme.Light,
    "Dark"  => AppTheme.Dark,
    _       => AppTheme.Unspecified
};
```

### ⚠️ Critical Android Pitfall

Your `MainActivity` **must** include `ConfigChanges.UiMode` or the `RequestedThemeChanged` event won't fire — Android will restart the activity instead:

```csharp
[Activity(Theme = "@style/Maui.SplashTheme",
          MainLauncher = true,
          ConfigurationChanges = ConfigChanges.ScreenSize
                               | ConfigChanges.Orientation
                               | ConfigChanges.UiMode  // ← Required!
                               | ConfigChanges.ScreenLayout
                               | ConfigChanges.SmallestScreenSize
                               | ConfigChanges.Density)]
public class MainActivity : MauiAppCompatActivity { }
```

Without this, toggling dark mode in Android settings causes a full activity restart, losing navigation state.

### Quick Summary

| Goal | API |
|---|---|
| Read current theme | `Application.Current.RequestedTheme` |
| React to changes | `RequestedThemeChanged` event |
| Force a theme | `Application.Current.UserAppTheme = AppTheme.Dark` |
| Follow system again | `UserAppTheme = AppTheme.Unspecified` |
| Persist user choice | `Preferences.Set` / `Preferences.Get` |
